Austere (aw-STEER)
Meaning: simple and strict
Hindi: सादा / कठोर
Example: The teacher lived an austere life.*


Cognizant (KOG-nuh-zuhnt)
Meaning: aware or conscious
Hindi: जागरूक
Example: She is cognizant of the risks.*


Disseminate (di-SEM-uh-nayt)
Meaning: to spread information
Hindi: फैलाना / प्रसारित करना
Example: The internet disseminates knowledge quickly.*


Eloquent (EL-uh-kwuhnt)
Meaning: fluent and persuasive in speaking
Hindi: वाक्पटु
Example: He delivered an eloquent speech.*


Frugal (FROO-guhl)
Meaning: careful with money
Hindi: मितव्ययी
Example: My grandfather is very frugal.*


Hypocrisy (hi-POK-ruh-see)
Meaning: pretending to have morals you do not follow
Hindi: पाखंड
Example: People criticized his hypocrisy.*


Immaculate (ih-MAK-yuh-lit)
Meaning: perfectly clean or flawless
Hindi: बेदाग / स्वच्छ
Example: Her room was immaculate.*


Nostalgia (no-STAAL-juh)
Meaning: sentimental feeling about the past
Hindi: पुरानी यादों की भावना
Example: The song filled him with nostalgia.*


Pragmatic (prag-MAT-ik)
Meaning: practical and realistic
Hindi: व्यावहारिक
Example: She took a pragmatic approach.*


Resilient (ri-ZIL-yuhnt)
Meaning: able to recover quickly
Hindi: लचीला / जल्दी संभलने वाला
Example: Children are often resilient after difficulties.*

